{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-1","title":"Ezekiel 36:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The land of Israel is comforted, both by destruction of the heathen, who spitefully used it, 8 and by the blessings of God promised unto it. 16 Israel was rejected for their sin, 21 and shall be restored without their desert. 25 The blessings of Christ's kingdom.</p>\n<p>the mountains. 6:2,3; 33:28; 34:14; 37:22 hear. 4,8; 20:47; 37:4; Jer 22:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-2","title":"Ezekiel 36:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Because. 5; 25:3; 26:2 even. De 32:13; Ps 78:69; Isa 58:14; Hab 3:19 our's. 35:10; Jer 49:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-3","title":"Ezekiel 36:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Because. Heb. Because for because. 13:10; Le 26:43 they have made. Jer 39:1-18; 41:1-18; 52:1-34; La 1:1-5:22 swallowed. Ps 35:25; 61:1; Pr 1:12; Jer 51:34; La 2:2,5,16 and ye. De 28:37; 1Ki 9:7,8; Ps 44:13,14; 79:10; Jer 18:16; 24:9; 33:24 La 2:15; Da 9:16 taken up in the lips of talkers. or, made to come upon thelip of the tongue. and are. Job 30:1-10; Ps 35:15,16; 69:12; Mt 27:39-44; 1Co 4:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-4","title":"Ezekiel 36:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>mountains. 1,6; De 11:11 rivers. or, bottoms, or dales. desolate. 33-35; 6:14; 2Ch 36:17-21; Isa 6:11; 24:1-12 a prey. 34:28; Ps 79:4; Isa 64:10,11; Jer 25:9-13; 29:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-5","title":"Ezekiel 36:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Surely. 38:19; De 4:24; Isa 66:15,16; Zep 3:8; Zec 1:15 against the. 3; Jer 25:9,15-29; Zep 2:8-10 against all. 25:8-14; 35:1-15; Ps 137:7; Isa 34:1-17; 63:1-6; Jer 49:7-22 La 4:21; Am 1:11,12; Ob 1:1-9; Mal 1:2-4 appointed. 35:10-12; Ps 83:4-12; Jer 49:1 with the. 35:15; Pr 17:5; 24:17,18; Ob 1:12; Mic 7:8 with despiteful. 25:12,15; Am 1:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-6","title":"Ezekiel 36:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>4,5,15; 34:29; Ps 74:10,18,23; 123:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-7","title":"Ezekiel 36:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I have lifted. 20:5,15; De 32:40; Re 10:5,6 the heathen. 25:1-35:15; Jer 25:9,15-29; 47:1-51:64; Am 1:1-15; Zep 2:1-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-8","title":"Ezekiel 36:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>ye shall. 34:26-29; Ps 67:6; 85:12; Isa 4:2; 27:6; 30:23; Ho 2:21-23 Am 9:13-15 for.The Edomites, and other enemies of the Jews, who thought they would soon be in possession of the whole land of Judea, might be assured that the predicted seventy years of the captivity were wearing away, and the time would soon arrive when the Jews would repossess and cultivate their own land, and eat its fruits.</p>\n<p>at hand. 12:25; Php 4:5; Heb 10:37; Jas 5:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-9","title":"Ezekiel 36:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Ps 46:11; 99:8; Ho 2:21-23; Joe 3:18; Hag 2:19; Zec 8:12 Mal 3:10,11; Ro 8:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-10","title":"Ezekiel 36:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>I will. 37; Isa 27:6; 41:17-23; Jer 30:19; 31:27,28; 33:12; Zec 8:3-6 the wastes. 33; Isa 51:3; 52:9; 58:12; 61:4; Jer 31:10-14; Am 9:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-11","title":"Ezekiel 36:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I will multiply. Jer 31:27; 33:12 and I will settle.The circumstances of the Jews were never so prosperous after the captivity as they had been before; hence this prophecy must refer to the times of the Gospel and the future conversion and restoration of the Jews.</p>\n<p>Jer 30:18; 31:38-40; Ob 1:19-21; Mic 7:14 will do. 35; Isa 30:26; 54:7-10; Jer 23:5-8; Joe 3:18-21; Am 9:15; Hag 2:6-9 Zec 8:11-15; Heb 8:8-13; 11:40 and ye. 35:9; 37:6,13; Isa 52:4-6; Ho 2:20; 1Jo 5:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-12","title":"Ezekiel 36:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>I will cause.The prophet is still personifying the mountains, valleys, and wastes of Judea.</p>\n<p>they shall. Jer 32:15,44; Ob 1:17-21 no more. 13; Nu 13:32; Jer 15:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-14","title":"Ezekiel 36:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>no more. 37:25-28; Isa 60:21; Am 9:15 bereave. or, cause to fail.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-15","title":"Ezekiel 36:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>men. 6; 34:29; Isa 54:4; 60:14; Mic 7:8-10; Zep 3:19,20 thou bear. Ps 89:50; Zep 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-17","title":"Ezekiel 36:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>they defiled. Le 18:24-28; Nu 35:33,34; Ps 106:37,38; Isa 24:5; Jer 2:7; 3:1,2,9 Jer 16:18; Mic 2:10 as the. Le 15:19-33; Isa 64:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-18","title":"Ezekiel 36:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>I poured. 7:8; 14:19; 21:31; 2Ch 34:21,26; Isa 42:25; Jer 7:20; 44:6; La 2:4 La 4:11; Na 1:6; Re 14:10; 16:1-21 for the. 16:36-38; 23:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-19","title":"Ezekiel 36:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>I scattered. 5:12; 22:15; Le 26:38; De 28:64; Am 9:9 according to their way. 7:3,8; 18:30; 22:31; 39:24; Ro 2:6; Re 20:12-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-20","title":"Ezekiel 36:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>they profaned.The Jews, when thus scattered, appeared to them an abject and wretched company of people. They were recognized as the worshippers of Jehovah wherever they went; but they were looked upon as a viler and more worthless race than any of the idolaters among whom they were driven. Many would ascribe their wickedness to the tendency of their religion, which they abhorred, and not to their having acted inconsistently with it; and regard their miseries, not as the punishment of their sins, but as proofs of God's inability to protect them. This profanation of his holy name, Jehovah was determined to wipe away, by shewing mercy unto them.</p>\n<p>Isa 52:5; Ro 2:24 These. Ex 32:11-13; Nu 14:15,16; Jos 7:9; 2Ki 18:30,35; 19:10-12 Jer 33:24; Da 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-21","title":"Ezekiel 36:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>20:9,14,22; De 32:26,27; Ps 74:18; Isa 37:35; 48:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-22","title":"Ezekiel 36:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>32; De 7:7,8; 9:5-7; Ps 106:8; 115:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-23","title":"Ezekiel 36:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>sanctify. 20:41; 38:22,23; Nu 20:12,13; Ps 46:10; Isa 5:16; 1Pe 3:15 and the heathen. 39:28; Ex 15:4-16; Ps 102:13-16; 126:1-3; Da 2:47; 3:28,29; 4:2,3 Da 4:34-37; 6:26,27 when I shall. 28:22; 1Pe 2:9 their. or, your.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-24","title":"Ezekiel 36:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>11:17; 34:13; 37:21,25; 39:27,28; De 30:3-5; Ps 107:2,3 Isa 11:11-16; 27:12,13; 43:5,6; Jer 23:3-8; 30:3,18; 31:8; 32:37 Jer 50:17-20; Ho 1:11; Am 9:14,15; Ro 11:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-25","title":"Ezekiel 36:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>will I. Le 14:5-7; Nu 8:7; 19:13-20; Ps 51:7; Isa 52:15; Joh 3:5; Tit 3:5,6 Heb 9:13,14,19; 10:22; 1Jo 5:6 filthiness. 17,29; 37:23; Ps 51:2; Pr 30:12; Isa 4:4; Jer 33:8; Zec 13:1 Ac 22:16; 1Co 6:11; 2Co 7:1; Eph 5:26,27; Tit 2:14; 1Jo 1:7; Re 1:5 Re 7:14 from all your idols. Isa 2:18-20; 17:7,8; Jer 3:22,23; Ho 14:3,8; Zec 13:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-26","title":"Ezekiel 36:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>new heart. De 30:6; Ps 51:10; Jer 32:39; Joh 3:3-5; 2Co 3:18; 5:17; Ga 6:15 Eph 2:10; Re 21:5 the stony. 11:19,20; Zec 7:12; Mt 13:5,20,21; Mr 4:16,17; 2Co 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-27","title":"Ezekiel 36:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>I will. 37:14; 39:29; Pr 1:23; Isa 44:3,4; 59:21; Joe 2:28,29; Zec 12:10 Lu 11:13; Ro 8:9,14-16; 1Co 3:16; Ga 5:5,22,23; Eph 1:13,14 2Th 2:13; Tit 3:3-6; 1Pe 1:2,22; 1Jo 3:24 cause. 37:24; Jer 31:33; Ga 5:16; Col 2:6; Php 2:12,13; Tit 2:11-14 Heb 13:21; 1Jo 1:6,7; 2Jo 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-28","title":"Ezekiel 36:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>dwell. 10; 28:25; 37:25; 39:28 be people. 11:20; 37:23,27; So 6:3; Jer 30:22,23; 31:33; 32:38; Ho 1:10 Zec 13:9; Mt 22:32; 2Co 6:16-18; 7:1; Heb 8:10; 11:16; Re 21:3,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-29","title":"Ezekiel 36:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>save. 25; Jer 33:8; Ho 14:2,4,8; Joe 3:21; Mic 7:19; Zec 13:1; Mt 1:21 Joh 1:7-9; Ro 6:14; 11:26; Tit 2:14 call. 8,9; 34:27-29; Ps 105:6; Ho 2:21-23; Mt 6:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-30","title":"Ezekiel 36:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>reproach. De 29:23-28; Joe 2:17,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-31","title":"Ezekiel 36:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>shall ye. 6:9; 16:61-63; 20:43; Le 26:39; Ezr 9:6-15; Ne 9:26-35 Jer 31:18-20; Da 9:4-20 shall lothe. Job 42:6; Isa 6:5; 64:6; Zec 12:10,11; Lu 18:13; Ro 6:21 2Co 7:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-32","title":"Ezekiel 36:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>for your. 22; De 9:5; Da 9:18,19; 2Ti 1:9; Tit 3:3-6 be ashamed. 16:63; Ezr 9:6; Ro 6:21; 1Pe 4:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-33","title":"Ezekiel 36:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>cause. Zec 8:7,8 wastes. 10; Isa 58:12; Jer 32:43; 33:10; 50:19,20; Am 9:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-34","title":"Ezekiel 36:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>6:14; De 29:23-28; 2Ch 36:21; Jer 25:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-35","title":"Ezekiel 36:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>they shall. Ps 58:11; 64:9; 126:2; Jer 33:9 like the. 37:13; Ge 2:8,9; 13:10; Isa 51:3; Joe 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-36","title":"Ezekiel 36:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>know. 17:24; 34:30; 37:28; 39:27-29; Mic 7:15-17 I the Lord have. 22:14; 24:14; 37:14; Nu 23:19; Ho 14:4-9; Mt 24:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-37","title":"Ezekiel 36:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>I will yet. 14:3; 20:3,31; Ps 10:17; 102:17; Isa 55:6,7; Jer 29:11-13; 50:4,5 Zec 10:6,9; 13:9; Mt 7:7,8; Php 4:6; Heb 4:16; 10:21,22; Jas 4:2,3 1Jo 5:14 I will increase. 10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-36-38","title":"Ezekiel 36:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>holy flock. Heb. flock of holy things. as the flock. Ex 23:17; 34:23; De 16:16; 2Ch 7:8; 30:21-27; 35:7-19; Zec 8:19-23 Ac 2:5-11 the waste. 33-35; 34:31; Jer 30:19; 31:27,28; Joh 10:16; Re 7:4-9</p>"}]}